# Banter in The Crooked Nightmare (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is crooked_nightmare): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ nm_estate_01_rook_delphine
if name:rook_coldwake and name:delphine_ravelle and at:nm_estate and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: We signed that house off as level, Delphine. Now it's forty degrees out and weeping purple muck.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Save your chalk. A house that bends and flashes red is staging a revival, not asking for a mason.
interject name:rook_coldwake: A revival still needs drainage. And my knocker hasn't stopped clacking since the signpost.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness just tried to rhyme clapboard with encore. More offensive than the screaming.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Nudge me if I forget to breathe before the porch. I hate clearing the same house twice.
endif
-> END

~ nm_dark_wood_02_tobin_silas
if name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and at:nm_dark_wood and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:tobin_hayward: White handprints slapped up the bark, Silas. Like a lunatic marking trees for felling.
interject name:silas_vane: And they lead straight to that crooked door. Somebody set this wood up for a very small player.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Look at the bite out of that stump. Clean through the heartwood.
interject name:silas_vane: My shadow's lagging a full stride under this blank moon. It only does that when the house is cheating.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep your cards in your fist and walk by the turnip light, then.
endif
-> END

~ nm_wedding_03_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:nm_wedding and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Animal masks in the dance ring and a black goat on the dais with the bride. In Picco that's extra.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Lively dancing. But the masked gentleman by the pole hasn't moved in ten minutes. And half the table is raw offal.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: If that goat starts taking vows, darling, I'm stealing the rose crown for my lining.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby is tucking his tail behind my boots, and there's not a whisper of thunder.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Keep your hand on his collar. Nobody sets a feast this big unless the guests are on the platter.
endif
-> END

~ nm_oven_04_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:nm_oven and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:cordelia_skein: This firebrick chamber could render someone to tallow in twelve minutes, Tobin. Look at that iron wheel.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Three paces between me and the grate. The draught's curling my cuffs, and my mice have gone still.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Hold still. I can spin a thin silk screen across you if the heat gets too much.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Save your thread for the woman chained to that top spit, before the crank turns her.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My vials are starting to simmer, Tobin. Let's be quick about the lock.
endif
-> END

~ nm_bookshelf_05_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:nm_bookshelf and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:rook_coldwake: No parapet on this plank, Lucan, and dust two inches deep. One bad step and that cat has us.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: At our present size, its teeth are the size of spades. Eight for vigilance. Its nose wants wiping.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Never mind the cat. There's a fellow up to his waist in a decanter the height of a watchtower.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Three parts cheap brandy, one part terror. Barnaby is barking at the book spines.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Keep the hound off the spilled spirits. My fingers are soft enough without climbing wet leather.
endif
-> END

~ nm_attic_06_tobin_delphine
if name:tobin_hayward and name:delphine_ravelle and at:nm_attic and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hold still, you're snagged on the stair nail, Delphine. That whole wall is a living pelt of vermin.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Never mind my stitches. Feathers in the cobwebs and a clawed pot boiling in a seven-pointed star.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Fifty years of sour ritual soaked into these boards. My head's itching with beetles just looking.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness isn't even making a pun about the crib. That's how bad it is.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Stay back from the cauldron and step round the chalk. Some rot you don't scrape off with a boot.
endif
-> END

~ nm_crater_07_tobin_lucan
if name:tobin_hayward and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:nm_crater and not flag.nm_chapter_done
interject name:tobin_hayward: I put a pinch of this ash on my tongue, Lucan. There's no earth in it at all.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The scent round the rim is burnt flat. And look across the bay. Thousands of lamps, and no chimney smoke.
interject name:tobin_hayward: I always said the soil never lies. Then this stone fell out of the sky and turned the roots to glass.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Barnaby won't go near that bench, if you please, and the hair on my own neck is rising.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Then let's see to the girl on the rim before that light gets into our seams.
endif
-> END

~ nm_estate_ruins_08_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and at:nm_estate_ruins and flag.crooked_house_destroyed
interject name:silas_vane: House always wins, unless you burn the house, Delphine. This one folded all the way to the cellar.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Curtain down, and not a rafter left to hang a drape from. Even Your Foolishness has gone quiet.
interject name:silas_vane: Clean sky over the dead tree, friend. Real stars, and no crone squinting at my tallies.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Not a brass button worth pocketing. Just broken timber, and a little girl by the porch steps.
interject name:silas_vane: Leave the trinkets. When the table clears this clean, you take your winnings and walk.
endif
-> END
